Show the workload as it actually runs, not as it was drawn

The README carried a mockup. The workload has been running inside Fabric
for some time now, so the screenshot is replaced with a capture of the
real thing: live connection status, counts read from the API rather than
invented, a CDC sample fetched from the engine, and the lineage graph
built from the saved links.

The asset is renamed accordingly. Calling a real screenshot "mockup"
would have been a small lie that outlived its reason, and the alt text
described panels that are not in the frame.

